{%- comment -%}
  The product page's lower accordions, from the theme's language files.

  Why here and not in the product's metafields: a metafield's Slovak lives in Translate & Adapt,
  which is STORE data — outside the repo, invisible in a diff, and impossible to preview before it
  is live. The language files make the two languages the same kind of object.

  Three slots, in this order:

    1. The product's own note — "How to read" on the tarot, "Reading it on a screen" on the
       Prague book. One lead and one shorter paragraph, which is the shape every product-page
       text takes (docs/design/COPY-GUIDE.md). Rendered only when <handle>_note_lead exists.
    2. As a gift — shared lead, shared text, and a per-product text when the shared one would be
       wrong. The stickers have no language, so "Pick the language they love to read in" cannot
       stand under them and they carry their own <handle>_gift_text.
    3. About Walter — shared, always the same under every product.

  Keys:
    walterin.product.<handle>_note_heading / _note_lead / _note_text
    walterin.product.<handle>_gift_text          optional override
    walterin.product.gift_heading / gift_lead / gift_text
    walterin.product.walter_heading / walter_lead / walter_text

  Every paragraph goes through wui-tail-nbsp so its last word is never left alone on a line
  (docs/design/LINE-BREAKS.md).

  Accepts: product (required), prefix (required, e.g. "walterin.product.tarot_")
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign note_lead = prefix | append: 'note_lead' | t
  assign has_note = true
  if note_lead contains 'Translation missing'
    assign has_note = false
  endif

  assign note_heading = prefix | append: 'note_heading' | t
  assign note_text = prefix | append: 'note_text' | t

  assign gift_text = prefix | append: 'gift_text' | t
  if gift_text contains 'Translation missing'
    assign gift_text = 'walterin.product.gift_text' | t
  endif
  assign gift_lead = 'walterin.product.gift_lead' | t
  assign walter_lead = 'walterin.product.walter_lead' | t
  assign walter_text = 'walterin.product.walter_text' | t
-%}

{%- if has_note -%}
  <details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
    <summary>
      <span class="wui-accordion__title">
        <span class="wui-label">{{ note_heading }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
      <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
        <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: note_lead -%}</p>
        {%- unless note_text contains 'Translation missing' -%}
          <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: note_text -%}</p>
        {%- endunless -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}

<details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
  <summary>
    <span class="wui-accordion__title">
      <span class="wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product.gift_heading' | t }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
    <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: gift_lead -%}</p>
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: gift_text -%}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

<details class="wui-accordion wui-accordion--suggest" data-wui-acc>
  <summary>
    <span class="wui-accordion__title">
      <span class="wui-label">{{ 'walterin.product.walter_heading' | t }}</span>
    </span>
    <span class="wui-accordion__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="wui-accordion__wrap">
    <div class="wui-accordion__body wui-rte">
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: walter_lead -%}</p>
      <p>{%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: walter_text -%}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
